const SEO = {"meta":{"og:title":"Pool Remodeling & Renovation Contractors in Florida","og:description":"Pool remodeling and renovation contractors in North & South Florida. Equipment upgrades, resurfacing, safety improvements, and efficiency.","og:image":"/images/obra/og/pool-remodeling-renovation-florida.jpg","twitter:title":"Pool Remodeling & Renovation Contractors in Florida","twitter:description":"Pool remodeling and renovation contractors in North & South Florida. Equipment upgrades, resurfacing, safety improvements, and efficiency.","twitter:image":"/images/obra/og/pool-remodeling-renovation-florida.jpg","og:type":"website","twitter:card":"summary_large_image"},"jsonLd":[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","about":{"@type":"Service","areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"Florida"}],"description":"Our pool remodeling contractors upgrade pools across North &amp; South Florida with modern finishes, energy-efficient variable-speed equipment, VGB-compliant safety features, and premium materials that dramatically improve both function and long-term app","image":"/images/obra/obra-048/pool-remodeling-travertine-deck-glass-tile-completed.avif","name":"Pool Remodeling","provider":{"@id":"https://www.mrandmrsoutdoorliving.com/#negocio","@type":"Organization","name":"Mr & Mrs Outdoor Living"},"serviceType":"Pool Remodeling & Renovation","url":"https://www.mrandmrsoutdoorliving.com/services/pool-remodeling"},"dateModified":"2026-05-18T19:55:49.094Z","datePublished":"2026-05-18T19:54:16.970Z","description":"Pool remodeling and renovation contractors in North &amp; South Florida. Equipment upgrades, resurfacing, safety improvements, and efficiency.","inLanguage":"en","mainEntity":{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pool remodeling improves efficiency, safety, appearance, and long-term property value, making Florida pools significantly easier to enjoy. Licensed under CPC1460562 and CPC1461119, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living handles the full scope — from structural inspection through final finish application."},"name":"Why remodel a pool in Florida?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the equipment being replaced and how the pool is run, so we do not quote a percentage. Variable-speed pumps are the biggest lever: they move the same water at lower speeds for most of the day, and Florida law (section 553.909, Florida Statutes) already requires residential pool pumps of 1 horsepower or more to run at two or more speeds. In a complete remodel we size the pump, filtration and low-voltage LED lighting to the renovated pool as one system, instead of swapping parts one at a time."},"name":"What energy savings can pool upgrades provide?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the scope: an interior refinish with new tile moves faster than a remodel that rebuilds the shell, replaces the equipment and redoes the deck. We assess the pool first and give you the schedule for your scope in writing, together with the fixed project price, before any demolition starts. Permit review and inspections are part of that schedule, and we coordinate them."},"name":"How long does a pool remodel take in Florida?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Pool renovations are an ideal time to add spas, tanning ledges, waterfalls, LED lighting, and smart automation systems. Our licensed pool contractors manage the permitting and installation of all additions alongside the renovation work, keeping your project coordinated and on schedule."},"name":"Can features be added during a pool renovation?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We connect Florida homeowners with lending partners, and the order matters: you get the scope of the renovation and a fixed project price in writing first, and only then review how to pay for it. Approval and terms come from the lender."},"name":"Do you offer financing options for outdoor projects?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is no single number: a remodel is priced from the condition of the shell, the finish and tile you choose, the equipment being replaced and the deck work around it. Our estimator walks you through those choices, and you get a fixed project price in writing before any demolition starts."},"name":"How much does a complete pool remodel cost in North Florida?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually, yes. Work that touches the structure, plumbing, electrical, equipment or the safety barrier is permitted and inspected under the Florida Building Code; resurfacing alone is treated differently by different jurisdictions. We confirm the scope with the building department and pull the permits under our license."},"name":"Does a pool remodel need a permit in Florida?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An assessment of the shell and plumbing, then the scope you choose: interior finish, waterline tile and coping, equipment and lighting, a spa added or rebuilt, deck resurfacing or replacement, and a code-compliant barrier, finished with start-up and a walk-through of the new equipment."},"name":"What is included in a complete pool remodel?"}]},"name":"Pool Remodeling","url":"/services/pool-remodeling"}]};
